{"Propagating ErrDeviceLimitReached from Authenticate directly will fail the anonymous authentication flow; consider whether the intended behavior is to allow the request but skip tagging (swallow the error and only log) or map it to a more appropriate HTTP-level response": 0.6529088616371155, "In updateDevice, returning ErrDeviceLimitReached when rowsAffected == 0 conflates multiple cases (nonexistent device, expired device, concurrent update); consider distinguishing these or renaming the error/adding logging": 0.41316843032836914, "In CreateOrUpdateDevice, the time range for CountDevices and updateDevice is recomputed with separate time.Now() calls, which may lead to subtle off-by-a-bit inconsistencies; capture now := time.Now().UTC() once and reuse it": 0.1474040448665619, "Avoid mutating the shared args slice across the DB session closure to prevent subtle bugs on retries or reuse - args is declared outside WithDbSession and then modified inside, which would keep appending query and parameters on retry or reuse": 0.557755172252655, "The anonymous device expiration constant is duplicated across packages (api/api.go and anonstore/database.go), which can cause divergence over time if only one is changed": 0.6476939916610718, "Add integration tests for AnonDeviceService when a non-zero AnonymousDeviceLimit is configured - current tests run with default AnonymousDeviceLimit of 0 so the new limit logic isn't covered through the service layer": 0.3922797739505768}